.TH OTPME-VLAN 1 "2026-07-26" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-vlan \- manage OTPme VLANs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-vlan
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIvlan\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-vlan
manages VLAN objects in the OTPme system. A VLAN object is the assignable
representation of a network VLAN. It is referenced by the
.B vlans
config parameter of sites, units, hosts, devices, users and tokens, and the
resulting value is returned as
.B Tunnel\-Private\-Group\-Id
during 802.1x or MAB port authentication.
.PP
Assigning a VLAN requires the
.B assign
ACL on the VLAN object. This makes VLAN assignment delegable per VLAN: an
operator can be allowed to hand out the guest VLAN without being able to put
anybody into the server VLAN.
.PP
VLANs are site local objects, but they can be assigned across sites by
prefixing the site name (\fIsite\fB/\fIvlan\fR). This is needed when users
are created on the master site only while each site runs its own VLANs.
.PP
An object can have one VLAN per site assigned, because an object may be used
at more than one site. The site answering the RADIUS request returns its own
VLAN. If none of the assigned VLANs belongs to it, it returns the first one
its
.B vlan_trusts
allow, in the order of those entries.
.PP
A cross site assignment is honoured only if the site answering the RADIUS
request lists it under
.BR vlan_trusts ,
as \fIsite\fR[\fB:\fIvlan_site\fR[\fB/\fIvlan\fR]] (see
.BR otpme (7)).
The VLAN is switched in that site's network, whichever site owns the VLAN
object, so that site decides. The
.B assign
ACL alone is not enough here, because it is checked by the site making the
assignment against its own copy of the VLAN, so a site holding the users
cannot put them into a VLAN of a network that did not agree.
.PP
A VLAN object carries an optional VLAN ID. If a VLAN ID is set it is sent to
the switch. Without a VLAN ID the VLAN name is sent instead, which is what
switches configured with named VLANs (e.g. Cisco) expect.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS VLAN Management
.TP
.B add \fIvlan\fR \fR[\fIvlan_id\fR]
Create a new VLAN, optionally with a VLAN ID.
.TP
.B del \fIvlan\fR
Delete a VLAN.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIvlan\fR]
Display VLAN information.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List VLANs, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIvlan\fR
Enable a disabled VLAN. A disabled VLAN is not handed out on authentication.
.TP
.B disable \fIvlan\fR
Disable a VLAN without deleting it.
.TP
.B rename \fIvlan\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a VLAN. Existing assignments are kept, because they reference the
VLAN by UUID.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIvlan\fR \fIunit\fR
Move VLAN to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIvlan\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS VLAN ID
.TP
.B vlan_id \fIvlan\fR \fR[\fIvlan_id\fR]
Set the 802.1Q VLAN ID (1-4094). Without \fIvlan_id\fR the VLAN ID is
removed and the VLAN name is sent to the switch instead.
.SS Policy Management
.TP
.B add_policy \fIvlan\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the VLAN.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIvlan\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the VLAN.
.TP
.B list_policies \fIvlan\fR
List policies attached to the VLAN.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIvlan\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry. Use the \fBassign\fR ACL to allow assigning
this VLAN to other objects.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIvlan\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B show_acls \fIvlan\fR
Display all ACLs for the VLAN.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIvlan\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIvlan\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-a\fR] [\fB\-d\fR] \fIvlan\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set, append to or delete a config parameter.
.TP
.B get_config \fIvlan\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show a config parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIvlan\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set VLAN description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIvlan\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIvlan\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIvlan\fR
Export VLAN configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIvlan\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all VLANs.
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving VLAN.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add guests 100
Create a VLAN with VLAN ID 100
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add printers
Create a VLAN without a VLAN ID. The name "printers" is sent to the switch.
.TP
.B otpme-vlan vlan_id guests 110
Change the VLAN ID
.TP
.B otpme-vlan add_acl guests role netadmins assign
Allow the role "netadmins" to assign this VLAN
.TP
.B otpme-token config joe/login vlans guests
Assign the VLAN to a token
.TP
.B otpme-host config myhost vlans berlin/guests
Assign a VLAN of another site to a host
.TP
.B otpme-site config berlin vlan_trusts master:berlin/guests
Allow objects of the site "master" to get the VLAN "guests" of berlin
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
